jobs.description:
SeqMatic is a Next Generation Sequencing (NGS) and omics services provider based in the San Francisco South Bay Area. The company was founded in 2012 by former Illumina R&D scientists who are experts in the NGS workflow and related bioinformatics.

We specialize in Illumina NGS platforms, bulk DNA/RNA-seq, Single-cell RNA, as well as custom sequencing services with fast turnaround times. Our lab is CLIA / CAP certified. We recently expanded our capabilities beyond RUO to support clinical trials for our Clients, in addition to incorporating novel technologies such as Spatial Transcriptomics, Epigenetics, Proteomics and Histopathology.

**About the Opportunity**

SeqMatic has a Research Associate position open to join our single cell sequencing services team. The position requires a strong background in molecular biology, particularly nucleic acid purification and NGS / Omics workflows. We offer a competitive salary, bonus, 401K matching, company lunch program, and medical/dental/vision benefits.

**Responsibilities include but are not limited to:**

* Sample accessioning using LIMS;
* Organize and maintain detailed experimental records and follow lab procedures
* Prepare cells and tissues using manual and automated protocols;
* Prepare sequencing libraries from single cells and nuclei using workflows from 10x Genomics and Parse Biosciences;
* Operate other common laboratory equipment such as thermocyclers, qPCR machines, and benchtop centrifuges;
* Organize and maintain detailed experimental records and follow lab procedures;
* Communicate in person and electronically with customers and team members

**Qualification Requirements:**

* Bachelor's degree in biology, Cell Biology, Molecular Biology, Biochemistry or a related science;

* 2+ years of hands-on experience working with cell and tissue cultures;
* 2+ years of hands-on experience performing cell and nuclei isolations using manual and automated methods such as from Miltenyi gentleMACS;
* 2+ years of hands-on experience of single cell library preparation (10x Genomics, Parse Biosciences, Takara SmartSeq, etc.);
* To support our “Onsite-seq” offering, occasional travel within 50 miles of our Fremont lab will be required;
* Must be highly detail-oriented and have strong lab and analytical skills;
* Experience working in clinical lab setting is preferred but not required;
* Solid English language communication skills;
* Ability to work well under pressure and to meet deadlines; accommodate a flexible schedule to support the workload;
* Ability to work independently and with a team;
* Must be legally authorized to work in the USA.
